### Problem

`test::test_mark_delivered_twice_succeeds` currently fails when actually run (`cargo test -p escrow`):

```
thread 'test::test_mark_delivered_twice_succeeds' panicked: called `Result::unwrap_err()` on an `Ok` value: Ok(())
```

The test calls `mark_delivered` twice and expects the second call to fail with `OrderNotPending` (guarded by `order.delivery_timestamp > 0`). But the test never calls `env.ledger().set_timestamp(...)`, so `env.ledger().timestamp()` stays at its default of 0 for both calls, `delivery_timestamp` is set to 0 on the first call, and the guard never trips — the second call succeeds instead of failing as asserted. In production this isn't exploitable (real ledger time is always greater than 0), but the test as written doesn't actually exercise the guard it claims to test, and currently just fails outright since nothing runs `cargo test` in CI to catch it (see companion CI-gap issue).

